 "coverage_qualification": [
  "The literal univalence hypothesis (no m-1 dimensional affine subspace of R^n contains the vertices) is equivalent to linear independence of the edges u_i-u_0 for 0<m<=n+1, and univalence holds. For n+1<m the hypothesis holds vacuously; the actual R^0, m=2 example (points (1/2,1/2) and (1/4,1/4) of C with the same image) proves that univalence then fails. This is a degenerate case of the literal wording, not an error of the printed statement; the intended hypothesis is affine independence.",
  "When zeta=0 the printed quotient zeta/|zeta| is undefined; f(C) is H^m null and the formalisation takes eta=0, so both sides of the density identity are zero."
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Published correction applied: erratum p. 7, book p. 384 line 19, the last factor of the wedge formula is <e_m, Df(x)>.",
  "Registered sources: the frozen source-preparation-v3 group with tactic, import and lexer repairs in twenty-seven files and the new SimplexAffinePlaneUnivalence; ledger 4.1.27/support/claude-repair-ledger-v1. Every frozen declaration header is literal except one qualified ordinal-scope header in UpperTriangularExteriorCoefficients.",
